# The *default* assumption for the VAULT is that things need to be tracked. The *only* exceptions to that sole assumption are **secrets** and **exhaust**. Tread lightly here.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HOW THIS FILE IS SHAPED, AND WHY IT LOOKS ODD
#
# Two rules of git that this file is built around:
#
#   1. A tracked file is NEVER ignored. Nothing below untracks anything that is
#      already committed; these patterns govern what can be added from here on.
#
#   2. Git does not descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, so a later `!` cannot
#      rescue a file inside one. `node_modules/` followed by `!**/*.md` loses
#      the markdown — silently.
#
# Rule 2 is why exhaust below is written `dir/**` (contents) plus `!dir/**/`
# (keep descending into subdirectories) instead of the usual `dir/`. That shape
# is what lets the markdown re-include at the bottom actually work. 49 markdown
# files are tracked inside node_modules today; the vault tracks markdown
# everywhere, and that is preserved deliberately.
#
# Verify a change here, do not eyeball it:
#
#     git check-ignore --no-index -v <path>     # why is this ignored?
#     git status --porcelain                    # did anything stop being seen?
#
# `--no-index` matters: without it, an already-tracked file always reports as
# NOT ignored, which makes a broken pattern look like it works.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# === SECRETS ===============================================================
# File patterns only — never a bare directory — so nothing here can shadow a
# markdown file by making git skip a whole tree.

# Environment files
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.template
.envrc
*.env
!**/*.example.env

# Private keys and certificates
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa
id_rsa.*
id_ecdsa
id_ecdsa.*
id_ed25519
id_ed25519.*
*.ppk

# Credential and token files
credentials.json
.credentials.json
application_default_credentials.json
token.json
tokens.json
oauth*.json
client_secret*.json
auth.json
.netrc
.pgpass

# Tool auth state
.claude/.credentials.json
.codex/auth.json
.mcp.json
.mcp-auth/
.op/*.env
.aws/credentials
.ssh/id_*
!.ssh/id_*.pub

# Bulk secret exports and recovery codes must never enter the public record.
secrets/
archive-secrets-*.json
*recovery-codes*
*.kdbx


# === EXHAUST ===============================================================
# Machine churn: dependency installs, caches, build output, local runtime state.
# Written as `dir/**` + `!dir/**/` so git keeps descending and the markdown
# re-include at the bottom still applies. See the note at the top.

# A pattern containing a slash is anchored to THIS directory, so `node_modules/**`
# would only match a copy at the repo root — `THE-GEMSTONE/node_modules/` would
# escape it. Tool directories therefore get a `**/` prefix to match at any depth.
#
# Names that are ALSO ordinary vault folders (build, dist, logs, tmp, .cache —
# 83 tracked files live under such paths) are anchored with a leading `/` to the
# repo root instead. Track-by-default means a note folder called `logs` three
# levels down is content, not exhaust.

# Dependency installs — unambiguous, any depth
**/node_modules/**
!**/node_modules/**/
**/.venv/**
!**/.venv/**/
**/venv/**
!**/venv/**/

# Python caches — unambiguous, any depth
**/__pycache__/**
!**/__pycache__/**/
*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/**
!**/*.egg-info/**/
**/.pytest_cache/**
!**/.pytest_cache/**/
**/.mypy_cache/**
!**/.mypy_cache/**/
**/.ruff_cache/**
!**/.ruff_cache/**/
**/htmlcov/**
!**/htmlcov/**/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml

# Build output — root only; `build`/`dist` are also legitimate vault folder names
/dist/**
!/dist/**/
/build/**
!/build/**/

# OS and editor droppings
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Logs and local runtime state — root only, same reason as build/dist
*.log
/logs/**
!/logs/**/
/.cache/**
!/.cache/**/
/tmp/**
!/tmp/**/


# === THE VAULT'S OWN RULE ==================================================
# Markdown is the vault. It is tracked wherever it lives, including inside the
# exhaust above. This is the last word on purpose — in git, the last matching
# pattern wins, so this overrides everything before it.
#
# It cannot rescue a file from an excluded *directory*, which is exactly why no
# rule above excludes a bare directory. Do not "simplify" `dir/**` + `!dir/**/`
# back to `dir/` without re-running the check-ignore commands at the top.
!**/*.md
!*.md

# ESTO PERPETUA!
